{"term":"team","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0cb04f1eff17610e7d","definition":"A set of draught animals, such as two horses in front of a carriage.","example":"It happened almost every day that coaches stuck fast, until a team of cattle could be procured from some neighbouring farm to tug them out of the slough.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion team","factory team","farm team","fireteam","first team","foreteam","go team","go-team","home team","interteam","intrateam","joint investigation team","kill team","loveteam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:88cd089adec8059f85","definition":"Any group of people involved in the same activity, especially sports or work.","example":"We need more volunteers for the netball team.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion team","factory team","farm team","fireteam","first team","foreteam","go team","go-team","home team","interteam","intrateam","joint investigation team","kill team","loveteam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:19b5d63f5bdfc12e7d","definition":"A group of animals moving together, especially young ducks.","example":"she will wonder to have a teeme of ducklings about her","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion team","factory team","farm team","fireteam","first team","foreteam","go team","go-team","home team","interteam","intrateam","joint investigation team","kill team","loveteam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c6a6379fb9945be1e","definition":"A royalty or privilege granted by royal charter to a lord of a manor, of having, keeping, and judging in his court, his bondmen, neifes, and villains, and their offspring, or suit, that is, goods and chattels, and appurtenances thereto.","example":"TEAM, Theam, Tem, Them. Sax. [from tyman, to propagate, to teem.] In old English law. Literally, an offspring, race or generation. A royalty or privilege granted by royal charter to a lord of a manor, of having, keeping and judging in his court, his bondmen, neifes and villeins, and their offspring or suit. They who had a jurisdiction of this kind, were said to have a court of Theme... constantly used in the old books in connection with toll, in the expression Toll & Team.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, obsolete","register":"UK, obsolete","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion team","factory team","farm team","fireteam","first team","foreteam","go team","go-team","home team","interteam","intrateam","joint investigation team","kill team","loveteam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a17ec9ee65908d0bc","definition":"A group of people who favor one side of a binary debate that is divided and lacks a well-established clear consensus.","example":"As Jan. 1, 2020, approaches, it turns out there is a Team Zero and a Team 1 – those who believe the new decade will begin after midnight on the upcoming New Year's Eve and those who believe the burgeoning celebrations of a new decade (and all the \"last decade\" retrospectives) are in fact a year early.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion team","factory team","farm team","fireteam","first team","foreteam","go team","go-team","home team","interteam","intrateam","joint investigation team","kill team","loveteam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a4748962430b05464","definition":"To form a group, as for sports or work.","example":"They teamed to complete the project.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["team up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["A team","away team","bat for the other team","blue team","B team","bubble team","Cinderella team","country team","crack team","crash team","crisis response team","cyberteam","dog team","don't change a winning team","double team","dream team","expansion